I mean, whoa. Whoa. That supposedly non-sapient sword just skidded
along the ground, then suddenly leaped from the ground, rocketed
straight up to the jabberwock's neck (jabberwocks can fly, by the way),
sliced clean through its spine in midair all by itself, and then just
fell back down to the floor, inert, innoculous.

And this ISN'T an intelligent artifact?! Why, this self-propelled skean
could match wits with Excalibur itself! Its sheer determination to seek
out and bisect necks of all kinds beats out even Stormbringer's
bloodlust!

Of course, this example does point out a rather esoteric bug:
BUG: flying enemies can be hit by kicked objects. Sure, one could
attempt to punt a sufficiently large crystal ball, but there's no way
you can get something as un-aerodynamic as a mace airborne with even a
swift kick.



